--TEST--
An `rule:types/object-literal` object literal writing one field name twice is `E0494` where it is written, at every depth and once per repeat, while the same braces spelling an `rule:core-api/shape-rules` R2 options bag keeps its own `E0304`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A shape's fields are a set: `{a: int}` names one slot, so the second `a`
// has nowhere to land. The interned shape reads the first of the pair and
// the class `nvs-ir` synthesizes would keep the last, which is exactly the
// silent disagreement this refuses.
var $twice = {a: 1, a: 2};
// Every repeat is named, not just the first one: three writes of `b` are
// two mistakes.
var $thrice = {b: 1, b: 2, b: 3};
// A literal nested inside another is an ordinary initializer, so the inner
// one is checked by the same rule at its own depth.
var $nested = {outer: {inner: 1, inner: 2}};
// `rule:core-api/shape-rules` R2's options bag is written with the same braces and is *not*
// this rule: a repeated option is `E0304` at the argument checker, which
// resolves each key against the member's own row rather than interning a
// shape. One spelling, two owners, and no diagnostic reported twice.
array<int> $rows = [1];
echo Core\Json::encode($rows, {pretty: true, pretty: false}), "\n";
echo "unreached\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0494]: the field `a` is written twice in this object literal
  --> %s:6:21
  |
6 | var $twice = {a: 1, a: 2};
  |                     ^ already given a value above
  = help: a shape's fields are a set, so there is one slot per name — drop one of the two, or give the second field its own name

error[E0494]: the field `b` is written twice in this object literal
  --> %s:9:22
  |
9 | var $thrice = {b: 1, b: 2, b: 3};
  |                      ^ already given a value above
  = help: a shape's fields are a set, so there is one slot per name — drop one of the two, or give the second field its own name

error[E0494]: the field `b` is written twice in this object literal
  --> %s:9:28
  |
9 | var $thrice = {b: 1, b: 2, b: 3};
  |                            ^ already given a value above
  = help: a shape's fields are a set, so there is one slot per name — drop one of the two, or give the second field its own name

error[E0494]: the field `inner` is written twice in this object literal
   --> %s:12:34
   |
12 | var $nested = {outer: {inner: 1, inner: 2}};
   |                                  ^^^^^ already given a value above
   = help: a shape's fields are a set, so there is one slot per name — drop one of the two, or give the second field its own name

error[E0304]: the option `pretty` is given twice
   --> %s:18:46
   |
18 | echo Core\Json::encode($rows, {pretty: true, pretty: false}), "\n";
   |                                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ already set above

